Release Notes AM335x-PD19.1.0
=============================

- Linux Kernel v4.14.78
- Linux Kernel v4.14.78-rt47 (PREEMPT_RT)
- barebox 2018.11.0
- Yocto 2.5.2 (sumo HEAD commit 623b77885051)
- Qt 5.9

Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------

  see machines.txt

Build Environment:
------------------

  - Ubuntu 16.04 64Bit

New Features:
-------------

  - Updated to kernel 4.14
  - Added support for rauc
  - Added support for phyBOARD-REGOR RUN/STOP LEDs
  - Added support for user LEDS on PCM-953 with PCM-062
  - Added update script (bbu.sh) to update MLO and barebox from userspace

Defeatured:
-----------

  - Removed phyboard-wega-am335x-4 support

  - USB OTG support has been removed. (Has been also de featured from upstream
    Kernel v4.18). USB as device and USB as host are still working but
    automatic switching isn't.

Known Issues:
-------------

  - phycore-am335x-som / phycore-r2-am335x-som:
         * Boot tests showed in about 2 of 2000 boots that the SMSC LAN8710 phy
	   could not be found. The PHY ID readout is wrong. The generic
           PHY driver will take over. Ethernet is still functional in this case.

  - phycore-am335x/phycore-r2-am335x:
         * rtc1 (AM335x RTC) has high deviation

  - CAN tests with 20kbit/s did not run successfully. All other CANopen
    standard bit rates are working. This can be fixed by switching the clock
    from 25 to 24 Mhz, but new problems with other components can occur.

  - PCM-953/phyBOARD-WEGA audio: Recording does not work correctly.

  - UART0 RXD does not work correctly in linux in 1 of 1000 boot cycles.
